		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4129&amp;p=31585#p31585"><![CDATA[
I use CPS on Windows 11 ARM (MacBook Pro M1 Pro w/ Parallels) and other than passing through the USB device to the Windows VM, it works with minimal effort.  No need to unload the ACM driver in this case.<br><br>I will say there was one issue I encountered and that was when I was trying to convert my radio (MD-UV390+) from stock firmware to OpenGD where I needed an Intel based Windows box to do the conversion.  It had to do with the programming cable drivers which were only provided for x86 systems.  After converting to the OpenGD firmware on the radio then I was able to do everything from within Windows 11 ARM without issue.<br><br>73,<br>Ryan AD2Q<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6258">ad2q</a> — Fri Jun 07, 2024 3:17 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
